 - Free Trial (40+)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/events/316801147/","description":"🎟️ **Registration is required in advance.**\n**Please note:** RSVP’ing on Meetup does **not** reserve your spot.\n[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=yP0NoWr) or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\n\nJoin us for **Kinetic Connections: Movement for Healthy Aging**, a welcoming movement and dance program for adults 40+ of all abilities.\nLooking for a supportive way to stay active, move with greater ease, and connect with others? **Kinetic Connections** offers a gentle and engaging approach to movement through music, breath awareness, imagination, and creative exploration.\n\nLed by instructor **Julia Sasso**, each class encourages you to move at your own pace and discover ways of moving that feel comfortable, enjoyable, and natural to you. Regular participation can help support balance, coordination, strength, flexibility, mobility, and overall well-being, while creating opportunities for creativity, self-expression, and social connection.\n\nNo previous dance experience is required. Whether you're returning to movement, looking for a new way to stay active, or simply want to enjoy moving in a welcoming environment, everyone is encouraged to participate in a way that feels right for them.\nCome curious, comfortable, and ready to move!\n\n## Event Details\n\n📍 **Location:** Miles Nadal JCC – 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n💃 **Format:** Guided movement and dance class\n👥 **Age:** 40+\n📅 **Session:** 6-week program\n⏱️ **Class length:** 60 minutes\n\n## What to Expect\n\n✔️ Gentle, accessible movement suitable for all abilities\n✔️ Guided exploration through music, breath, and imagination\n✔️ Movement at your own pace and comfort level\n✔️ Exercises that support balance, coordination, strength, flexibility, and mobility\n✔️ Opportunities for creativity and self-expression\n✔️ A welcoming environment that encourages connection and community\n✔️ No previous dance experience required\n\n## About the Instructor\n\n**Julia Sasso** has enjoyed a distinguished career as a performer, choreographer, and dance educator spanning several decades. Throughout her work, she has been passionate about helping people discover the benefits and joy of movement at every stage of life.\nJulia’s classes create a supportive space to explore movement, build confidence, and connect with others while encouraging curiosity, creativity, and overall well-being.\n\nWhether you’re looking to stay active, improve your mobility, reduce stress, try something new, or simply enjoy an hour of movement and connection each week, **Kinetic Connections** is a welcoming place to move, explore, and feel good.\nCome experience the joy of moving well! ✨","startDate":"2026-10-21T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave, Room 317b, M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316803367/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-21T20:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Magic the Gathering: Going Commander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/316803536/","description":"Every Wednesday Night!\nFree Magic The Gathering Commander games at Hairy Tarantula, hosted by Toronto Gaymers!\n\nPlease note: Masks are required in store!\n\nFor more information and to RSVP please over to harryt.com/events","startDate":"2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hairy Tarantula","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"3456 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Spanish Classes (In-Person)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/events/316803906/","description":"**Spanish in Mississauga - Introduction to Spanish**\nNew beginner Spanish language classes in Mississauga\n\nIn this class, we will explore the Spanish language through 8 modules. We will cover basic concepts which you need to know in any Spanish-speaking country, and we will begin speaking right away and practicing in groups by module 3.\n\nThe goal is that you gain a basic understanding of the language. Weekly homework is required and active participation is encouraged.\n\n**These classes are not free.** Please consider watching an information session to learn more about the structure and how you can be part of this learning community.\n**Costs:** In-person registration can be made during the first class, and you can pay all classes at once without incurring payment fees (on this platform). You can also register for all classes right here on Eventbrite.\n\n**Date:** We will host weekly beginner Spanish classes weekly, for four (4) weeks:\n\n* October 7\n* October 14\n* October 21\n* October 28\n\nWe may offer a class social - practice in a group setting, restaurant or venue TBD.\nThis is your opportunity to learn language in only four classes!\n\n**Time**: Classes will begin at 5:30pm and will end at 6:30pm.\n\n**Location:** Mississauga Valley Community Centre\nClasses will be held in-person .\n\nPlease ensure that you participate in all four (4) classes, as we have already covered pronunciation and are practicing with our peers by class 2.\n\nIf you cannot attend all classes, consider joining us next month. We will continue to offer them on the first 4 Wednesdays of each month - participation in all classes is mandatory.\n\n**The instructor**\nMeet Rohit (Vic) Mehta- a fluent spanish speaker who has been a private tutor since 2014. He is continuing the popular Beginner Spanish Class series which was offered during pre-Covid times.\n\nWe hope to see you there! If you have any questions, please don't hesitate to contact us! Email dogoodspanish@gmail.com\n\n**Frequently Asked Questions:**\n\n**Do the classes have a cost?**\nYes, classes cost 20 each + fees (if paying online). You can also contribute cash or pay by interac e-transfer. There is an additional textbook available for purchase for 20.\n\n**How long are the classes?**\nClasses are held in-person for one (1) hour per week x 4 weeks. At the end of the weekly sessions, we will invite you to a social on a separate evening or weekend.\n\n**What should I bring?**\nA water bottle, snack, notebook and pen.\n\n**Is free parking available?**\nYes, the Mississauga Valley Community Centre has ample parking, and is also very accessible by transit.\n\n**Can I bring a friend?**\nYes absolutely, however all participants need to pay as an individual. We will credit you one (1) FREE class for bringing a friend.\n\n**Can I bring my kids?**\nNo, this is an adult only class. The themes are fast-paced and we want all participants to feel comfortable. We can make exceptions for older teenagers.\n\n**What if I miss a class?**\nIt is recommended that you attend all four (4) classes in the series. We can make a rare exception and offer a paid, Zoom class, for extreme circumstances.\n\n**What if I already took a beginner class?**\nConsider joining our Intermediate Class 4-part series, from 6:40pm to 7:40pm, beginning on the first Wednesday of each month.","startDate":"2026-10-21T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Mississauga Valley Community Centre, Hazel MacCallion Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1275 Mississauga Valley Blvd., ON L5A 3R8, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/"},"performer":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"GitHub Copilot Dev Days Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/events/316393717/","description":"**REGISTER AT [https://luma.com/5mthp0p6](https://luma.com/5mthp0p6)** instead of Meetup for this event\\*\\*.\\*\\* This event takes place at Microsoft Headquarters building which requires attendees to register using provided link to get QR code to a unique QR Code in order to enter the Microsoft Headquarters.\n\nPlanning is underway. RSVP now to reserve your spot. Space is limited.\n\nDev Days is a global, in-person, community-led experience bringing developers, DevOps enthusiasts, and local tech communities together to discover what’s possible with GitHub Copilot.\nThis isn’t your typical conference talk series. It’s a hands-on opportunity to explore real-world workflows, practical use cases, and the latest ways to put GitHub Copilot to work.\n\nJoin us for interactive demos, hands-on activities, and workshops focused on GitHub Copilot — and leave with practical skills, ideas, and techniques you can start using right away.\n\nCome curious. Get hands-on. Build something. See what GitHub Copilot can really do.\n\nEvent is co-hosted with Microsoft and North Toronto Cloud & DevOps User Group.","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Microsoft Canada HQ Downtown","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4400-81 Bay Street, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Green Drinks Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/to-sustainability/events/315710906/","description":"Hosted by [Green Drinks Toronto](http://www.greendrinks.org/ON/Toronto):\n\n*We will have a lively mixture of people from NGOs, academia, students, government and business. Come along and you'll be made welcome. Just say, \"are you green?\" and we will look after you and introduce you to whoever is there. It's a great way of catching up with people you know and also for making new contacts. Everyone invites someone else along, so there’s always... a different crowd, making Green Drinks an organic, self-organising network.*\n\n*These events are very simple and unstructured, but many people have found employment, made friends, developed new ideas, done deals and had moments of serendipity.*\n\n*GLOBAL: Now active in over 350 cities worldwide!*","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Lobster Burger Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"214 king st west,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Sustainability Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/to-sustainability/"},"performer":"Toronto Sustainability Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Coming Out, Being Out - Peer Discussion (Weekly)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/events/316804277/","description":"**Description**\n\nComing Out Being Out (COBO) is a peer discussion group that has served the LGBT community for over 15 years in downtown Toronto. We meet to share stories and opinions, challenges and triumphs at all stages of coming out and being out.\n\nCOBO participants are lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, two-spirit and questioning people. We welcome all who identify under the banner of queer sexual orientation and gender identity.\n\n**What We Do**\n\n\\|\\-\\| COBO participants are often seeking to:\n\n* Understand what experiences others have in coming out to family, friends and their respective communities.\n* Develop comfort in discussing their identity with others.\n* Meet others having the same experiences when it comes to living openly.\n* Receive the encouragement of peers.\n\n\\|\\-\\| Regular topics of discussion include:\n\n* How people choose to come out (at work, with family, with friends).\n* Where to find others like us in the community.\n* Challenges and triumphs in navigating family and partner relationships.\n\n**Where & When**\n\n* Every Wednesday from 6-8pm\n* Community meeting space at Casey House - 119 Isabella St., Toronto\n\n**How to Access the Meeting**\n\nRegistration on Meetup is not required to attend. Attendance is on a drop-in basis. The front door to our meeting space at Casey House is controlled by the main floor receptionist. To access the space when you arrive:\n\n* Press the button to the left of the main entrance door.\n* Tell the receptionist that you are there for the COBO meeting.\n* You will be buzzed in and someone from our group will come to show you to the meeting.\n\nWE LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING YOU ON WEDNESDAY!\n\n*COBO is a community group led by non-professional peer facilitators and is not a Casey House program.*","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Casey House - Community Meeting Space","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"119 Isabella Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/"},"performer":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Boxing Fundamentals (16+) — Build Strength & Skill | Fall 2026 Session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/events/316804282/","description":"**Fall 2026 Session**\n**Registration required in advance**\n**[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=xlZWnma)**\n☎️ Or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\n\n️ **Fees**\n• Full program session registration available\n• Prorated pricing if joining after the start date\n• Drop-in options may be available (space permitting)\n**Boxing Fundamentals (16+) at the Miles Nadal JCC**\n\nReady to build strength, sharpen your skills, and break a sweat? This no-contact beginner program introduces essential boxing fundamentals including stance, footwork, punches, bagwork, partner drills, and conditioning — all in a supportive and inclusive environment. No sparring involved.\n\nPerfect for new boxers or anyone looking to develop a strong foundation while improving fitness and confidence.\n\n**Led by Coach Nick Radionov — former Ukrainian National Olympic Boxing Team member, Level 3 Boxing Ontario–certified coach, and multi-time world kickboxing champion.**\n\n**Program Details**\n**Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter via Spadina doors)\n\n**What You’ll Learn & Benefit From**\n**Learn the Basics** — Develop proper form, movement, and striking technique\n**Build Strength & Stamina** — High-energy conditioning in every class\n**Train with Confidence** — Beginner-friendly instruction in a welcoming environment\n**Hands-On Skill Development** — Bagwork & partner drills (no-contact/no sparring)\n\n**What to Bring:** Handwraps, boxing gloves, indoor athletic shoes, and a water bottle.\n\nJoin us and build skill, strength, and confidence — one round at a time!","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave, Room 317b, M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Oral Conversational Spanish, English, and French Class 4 Adults!!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316804269/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI Clinic 02: Can AI actually do this? Bring the task and find out","url":"https://www.meetup.com/build-with-ai-mississauga/events/316064992/","description":"Everybody has a task they have quietly wondered about. The one where you think *surely a computer could do this by now*, and then you never find out, because asking felt like it would turn into a sales call.\n\nThis is where you ask.\n\nSame format every month. Everyone names one job they keep doing by hand, all of it goes on a board, and it gets sorted in front of the room into **do it yourself this week**, **a weekend project**, or **needs help, or leave it alone**. Then three or four get taken apart properly: the approach, the tool, roughly the cost, what breaks.\n\nEvery bottleneck in the room gets sorted out loud and gets a first step. Some of these are a ten minute job, some are a real project, and some are not worth doing. You will be told which.\n\nYou get a straight answer, including when the answer is no. Some things are not worth automating and you deserve to hear that too.\n\n**The night**\n\n* 6:00 Doors, coffee, write your bottleneck on a card\n* 6:15 Round the table, sixty seconds each\n* 6:35 The board\n* 6:50 Three or four worked through properly\n* 7:20 Networking\n* 8:00 Out\n\n**Who should come**\n\nAny owner or operator with a repetitive job and no idea whether it can be handed over. New faces and returning ones both, and if you came last month, bring the next one down your list.\n\n**What to bring**\n\nOne task, described specifically. No laptop.\n\n**Cost** Free.\n\n**When:** Wednesday 21 October 2026, 6:00 to 8:00 pm.\n\n**Where:** 30 Topflight Drive, Mississauga. Follow the signs to the offices when you arrive. Doors at 6:00, and it is worth being there for the round the table at 6:15 because that is where your bottleneck goes on the board.","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"30 Topflight Drive","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Topflight Dr., Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Build with AI, Mississauga","url":"https://www.meetup.com/build-with-ai-mississauga/"},"performer":"Build with AI, Mississauga"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Learn to dance Cha Cha & Rumba","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ballroom-and-latin-dancing-in-mississauga/events/316804106/","description":"💃 Learn to Dance Cha Cha & Rumba!\n\nJoin us for a fun and welcoming social dance class at D2R Studio. Learn the fundamentals, improve your rhythm, and dance with confidence while learning and having fun.\n\nRegister: $155 for 8 Weeks (1 class per week)\nor Drop In: $25\n\nBeginner-friendly and open to all levels.\n\n📍 392 Gibraltar Drive, Mississauga\n📞 Call or text: 647-202-6236\n🌐 dancetotherhythm.ca\n\nCome dance, have fun, and enjoy the music!\n\nHappy Dancing!","startDate":"2026-10-21T22:00:29.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Dance To The Rhythm Studio","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"392 Gibraltar Drive, (Upstairs, 2nd Floor), Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Salsa, Latin & Ballroom Dance Classes & Party in Mississauga","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ballroom-and-latin-dancing-in-mississauga/"},"performer":"Salsa, Latin & Ballroom Dance Classes & Party in Mississauga"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/c/1/2/highres_532904050.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/0/d/2/highres_533149362.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/4/b/f/highres_505678559.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/6/7/2/highres_536165746.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/0/a/f/highres_536037519.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/e/6/highres_515340486.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/0/a/0/highres_528881120.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/f/b/9/highres_530260889.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><meta name="next_csrf" content="4f538ca8-fe8f-46ad-b1d1-4b9b48fd1efa"/><script>(function(){try{if(typeof performance==="undefined"||!performance.getEntriesByType)return;var n=performance.getEntriesByType("navigation");if(!n||!n[0]||!n[0].name)return;var u=new URL(n[0].name);var h=u.hash||"";var m=h.match(/:~:text=([^&]+)/);if(m){window.__meetup_text_fragment__={hasTextFragment:true,textFragment:decodeURIComponent(m[1]).trim().slice(0,100),capturedAt:Date.now()}}else{window.__meetup_text_fragment__={hasTextFragment:false,capturedAt:Date.now()}}}catch(e){}})()</script><script>(function(){try{var hasCookie=document.cookie.split(';').some(function(c){return c.trim()==='isNativeApp=true'});var hasParam=window.location.search.indexOf('isNati